{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/957174-how-long-do-your-onyx-path-games-last","id":957174,"title":"How long do your Onyx Path games last?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-24T14:00:20-07:00","id":957174,"title":"How long do your Onyx Path games last?","content":"On average my groups campaign (or chronicle) last 9 sessions (or chapters) that take 4-5 hours. Is this normal, or do most people play longer/shorter games?<br /> <br /> I am especially interested in hearing from Onyx Path developers, and what you would recommend as a perfect Chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T14:19:24-07:00","id":957183,"title":"","content":"Pretty much. Start in the the evening, and 4-5 is about as much as people can do.<br /> Mind you, I used to play a lot of one-shots where the session would stretch to cover the material.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T14:27:33-07:00","id":957185,"title":"","content":"I tend to run 3-ish hour games, but when designing, I keep in mind that a lot of people do 4 or 5. My best <i>Vampire</i> campaign ran around eight episodes. (And it got me my first WW gig, so it was doubly successful!)<br /> <br /> The best game I was ever in was a <i>Changeling </i>campaign that ranged between 1 and 4 hours per session (we ran a lot of spontaneous scenes), and spanned dozens of sessions over five years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 08-24-2016, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T14:29:02-07:00","id":957187,"title":"","content":"We usually get a couple more hours than that in, but when things are busy in real life that's about it.<br /> <br /> Our games, unless planned ahead of time as short like our Vampire game, tend to last a long time. Changeling was twice a week for most of the time, from September in 2011 to December of 2013. Our vampire game was, ideally, just going to be a few months from when Vampire's second edition came out until Werewolf's second edition came out, but ended up stretching out plots and going from July of 2013 to November in 2014. Then Werewolf from March of 2015 through now.<br /> <br /> Pick-up games online I try to shoot for 6 hours but it ends up being erratic and the overall length of the chronicle is often cut short.<br /> <br /> If you look around the forum you can find links to some actual play podcasts or threads where you can see how long they go and sometimes the process of making them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T14:52:55-07:00","id":957199,"title":"","content":"About 10-15 sessions of 4 hours. These days I try to do a bunch of smaller chronicles. 3-4 sessions of 3-4 hours each.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T14:56:37-07:00","id":957204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/957174-how-long-do-your-onyx-path-games-last?p=957185#post957185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to run 3-ish hour games, but when designing, I keep in mind that a lot of people do 4 or 5. My best <i>Vampire</i> campaign ran around eight episodes. (And it got me my first WW gig, so it was doubly successful!)<br /> <br /> The best game I was ever in was a <i>Changeling </i>that ranged between 1 and 4 hours per session (we ran a lot of spontaneous scenes), and spanned dozens of sessions over five years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Always happy to hear from Rose Bailey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T15:01:15-07:00","id":957209,"title":"","content":"Sessions are about four hours, usually once a week. They can last for a full year or more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T15:26:14-07:00","id":957227,"title":"","content":"How do you make them last so long? Our campaigns revolve around a specific situation, do yours?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T15:26:17-07:00","id":957228,"title":"","content":"Exactly right now in this instant I'm running a CofD-powered solo game. We play about 3 hours per session, and this specific one is written in a google doc. We are at something like 200 pages right now, and we started 3 months ago.<br /> Normal games when they are on are usually 3 games per month, 6 hours long, when academic season is on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T15:39:17-07:00","id":957236,"title":"","content":"Let's see, I've got a doc chronicling all my arcs so let me just add up and see...<br /> <br /> Looks like I've run 7 one shots, 7 two shots, 11 three episode arcs, 9 four episode arcs and 4 five episode arcs. Though, many of those are sub arcs within longer running series. My longest running series were both ~35 episodes, with shorter ones clocking in around a dozen. Games average 4 - 5 hours, with the very occasional extra long 6+ hour game (though we've only ever had those at climaxes when no one wants to stop and break for two weeks).<br /> <br /> As a related note, we've also racked up 75 distinct player characters, in ~6 years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T15:44:37-07:00","id":957239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/957174-how-long-do-your-onyx-path-games-last?p=957236#post957236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's see, I've got a doc chronicling all my arcs so let me just add up and see...<br /> <br /> Looks like I've run 7 one shots, 7 two shots, 11 three episode arcs, 9 four episode arcs and 4 five episode arcs. Though, many of those are sub arcs within longer running series. My longest running series were both ~35 episodes, with shorter ones clocking in around a dozen. Games average 4 - 5 hours, with the very occasional extra long 6+ hour game (though we've only ever had those at climaxes when no one wants to stop and break for two weeks).<br /> <br /> As a related note, we've also racked up 75 distinct player characters, in ~6 years.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I'm not the only one that thinks of them as episodes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T15:45:54-07:00","id":957240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/957174-how-long-do-your-onyx-path-games-last?p=957228#post957228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly right now in this instant I'm running a CofD-powered solo game. We play about 3 hours per session, and this specific one is written in a google doc. We are at something like 200 pages right now, and we started 3 months ago.<br /> Normal games when they are on are usually 3 games per month, 6 hours long, when academic season is on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I used to think solo games were super weird, and maybe they are, but there is something great about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T15:46:21-07:00","id":957241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/957174-how-long-do-your-onyx-path-games-last?p=957239#post957239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I'm not the only one that thinks of them as episodes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I run a group of writers, actors and editors...in Los Angeles, so we certainly see it with a TV spin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T15:48:38-07:00","id":957243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/957174-how-long-do-your-onyx-path-games-last?p=957241#post957241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I run a group of writers, actors and editors...in Los Angeles, so we certainly see it with a TV spin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please tell me you got to work on an AMC show.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T15:54:22-07:00","id":957245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/957174-how-long-do-your-onyx-path-games-last?p=957227#post957227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you make them last so long? Our campaigns revolve around a specific situation, do yours?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well. There's usually a big arc and plot and then several minor arcs, at least one for each character at minimun. Then, I try to make things equal, so if one character had a couple of arcs devoted to them, I try to make it so the other also get their due. I must note my games are what one would call a sandbox. I have the place and the npc's solidly worked out (especially motivations and objectives) so they can react acordingly to the actions of the pcs without problem. Things keep moving even when the characters do nothing, as the npcs also act, so the world evolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T15:57:58-07:00","id":957246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/957174-how-long-do-your-onyx-path-games-last?p=957245#post957245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well. There's usually a big arc and plot and then several minor arcs, at least one for each character at minimun. Then, I try to make things equal, so if one character had a couple of arcs devoted to them, I try to make it so the other also get their due. I must note my games are what one would call a sandbox. I have the place and the npc's solidly so they can react acordingly to the actions of the pcs without problem. Things keep moving even when the characters do nothing, as the npcs also act, so the world evolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are the kinds of games our group plays. There is a main premises, and then the storyteller turns us loose while the NPC's go about their goals. We usually end up concluding the central conflict in 9 sessions, by then we want play something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T16:46:02-07:00","id":957267,"title":"","content":"I've run three campaigns all-up (weeeeeeeeell, kinda four?).<br /> <br /> Changeling was the first, which ran about a year. Had four central &quot;themes&quot; rather than discrete plots that changed with the seasons. It began in Winter with the players having escaped Arcadia, so the theme was finding safety in the Freehold and they had a lot of little adventures along those lines. In Spring the players were building their lives. In Summer war came to the Freehold, culminating in a showdown with the Wild Hunt. In Autumn the big True Fae looming over everything made its move, and they had to face their fears.<br /> <br /> Mummy was next. That game lasted sixteen months all-up, if I remember right. For that one I didn't even really try for an overarching plot, ran it as much as a pure sandbox as I could until we decided to move the game into gear for a finale.<br /> <br /> Mixed in with Mummy was a Deceived campaign running concurrently and overlapping at several important junctures. I think it went for 8-10 months, can't remember exactly.<br /> <br /> Most recently I ran a Demon game and went in the opposite direction, making it a rather directed campaign with a discrete story that unfolded in 8-9 sessions, so about two months in total.<br /> <br /> All of these games ran with a single session every week averaging about 4 hours in length.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T16:52:26-07:00","id":957271,"title":"","content":"5-6 hours, on saturday afternoons. From 13-18/19 with an extended invitation to get here at 12 and enjoy my fine cooking until 13.<br /> <br /> My campaigns usually last some months. I can do some 3-5 sessions long games but I'm not confortable with that. I like character-based stories so my players and I need some time to fully develop and enjoy a deep character. My &quot;lucky number&quot; is 25-30 sessions for character-based stories (<i>something</i> happening but focus on <b>how</b> you deal with it), 15-20 for campaign-based ones (focus on <b>what</b> is happening).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11854-dibastet","name":"DiBastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T17:11:01-07:00","id":957275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/957174-how-long-do-your-onyx-path-games-last?p=957240#post957240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I used to think solo games were super weird, and maybe they are, but there is something great about them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's weird, because most games are not built for the concept. Obviously things like Dungeons &amp; Dragons practically require a group. But as you get into World of Darkness some games, like Mummy or Promethean, are practically made for it. Other games can thrive with it. They're all still built for a standard group, but the fiction too usually revolves around what seems like single PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T17:21:47-07:00","id":957280,"title":"","content":"Our sessions are usually 3-4 hours long, and we can usually swing every other week (we aim for weekly, but we all have adult obligations). Chronicles are typically 12-18 months long, so maybe 25-40 chapters. Those are pretty sandbox-y games with most of my work done before the first session starts and everything that follows building on the foundation.<br /> <br /> Back when my wife ran games regularly (pre-children), we played weekly pretty reliably for 3-4 hours, and games lasted 2 to 3 1/2 years, which works out to 100-175 sessions. Let's just say that if there was a point where a game's mechanics broke down as XP totals got ridiculous, we eventually reached it...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T17:34:21-07:00","id":957284,"title":"","content":"My most recent <b>Vampire: The Requiem</b> chronicle &quot;<a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?734837-Vampire-The-Requiem-2nd-Edition-Nobody-Wants-You\" target=\"_blank\">Nobody Wants You</a>&quot; ran for an academic year (about nine months with gaps) because it was in a university society, with individual sessions of three to three and a half hours. It had a central premise but room for side plots and personal storylines for the players' characters, some of which took up the meat of a session, before a final run of sessions at the climax.<br /> <br /> My current <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b> game has run for two academic years and while it will be ending soon it could have continued. It has a central premise that advanced and changed every few months (outside vampires probing a large city's court for weaknesses, then a rival city court starting a guerilla war, then a factional conflict among the local elders...) as well as building in more room for side plots and personal storylines.<br /> <br /> And that's nothing compared to a more light-hearted urban fantasy game I ran for six years, partially because I could get away with sessions of the week like &quot;it's five years later and a post-apocalypse future&quot; and &quot;the werewolf player character splits into human and monster sides&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}